{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require paid dog walkers be insured, DBS-checked, trained & 18+ years old",
        "additional_details": "We believe being a dog walker is a massive responsibility and requires experience, training and an understanding of dogs to ensure the public\u2019s safety. \r\n \r\nWhilst we appreciate the motivation, drive and initiative of young people to walk dogs, we feel dog walking is not a job that can be done by a child or young person. \r\n \r\nUnder new legislation, paid dog walkers should be required to have insurance, be DBS checked, and trained in first aid and being able to responsibly and confidently handle potential risks, such as dog attacks, dog theft, and other risks that may challenge adults.",
        "background": "We would like the Government to legally require all paid dog walkers to be 18 years old and above, properly trained and DBS-checked, and ban any children or young people under 18 from being paid dog walkers.  ",
